    18	## 1. Question, arms, estimands, hypotheses
    19	
    20	**Question (Yixun).** Does *input canonicalization* — before every model input, at training and at inference, cyclically shift the depth panorama horizontally so that the deepest pixel's column is the leftmost column (poses co-rotated) — make the generated RIR invariant to horizontal cyclic shifts of the panorama, and how does its clean performance compare with vanilla P1, FA B-F (OrbitRIR) and Yaw-Aug at the identical recipe and budget?
    21	
    22	**Arms.** `CANON` (new training run) vs the three existing 40k endpoints (P1, B-F, YAW; NAS-pinned shas above). CANON = P1's config plus `training.canonicalize` (§3): a **single intended config/algorithm delta against a historical matched-recipe control** (review H7) — P1 trained at `e50d098`, CANON trains at the exp_25 pin; §7 lists the static training-path diff audit that bounds the residual. Not a strict contemporaneous causal pair; wording in §9 reflects that.
    23	
    24	**Estimands** (full published unseen split unless stated; EMA weights, cfg 1.0, 1 Euler step, `--cond-autocast bf16`, `--cond-method vanilla`, K ∈ {1, 8} via the existing `acousticroom_unseeneval{_1,}.json`; every generative cell also records its assignment stream and dumps its scored waveforms, §5):
    25	
    26	- `m_Z(a, K)` — **Table block**: θ = 0, eval seeds 42–46; T60, C50, EDT, R@1/5/10, FD; item-weighted mean ± sd (the table's estimand) and the per-scene mean recorded. Arms `a ∈ {CANON, P1, YAW}` measured at ONE evaluator pin (B-F: historical row, fa eval; see §5 ledger).
    27	- **Invariance of CANON, three tiers (review B3):**
    28	  - **Tier 1 — structural (exact):** for every item of a rotated cell (C4, 45°, random yaw) the sha256 of the *canonical recovered-depth image* equals the one of the same item in the θ=0 cell with the same seed and K: **6,337 / 6,337 equal**, by construction of §2.1 (the roll is integer arithmetic on a bitwise-stable proxy). Recorded in the `.canon.json` sidecar.
    29	  - **Tier 2 — waveform (numerical):** paired per-item relative L2 and L∞ between the scored waveforms of a rotated cell and its θ=0 pair (identical eval seed ⇒ identical generative noise and context draw, proven by identical `input_hash`): pre-registered PASS if `median ≤ 1e-3`, `p99 ≤ 1e-2`, `max ≤ 1e-1`, each judged against the **repeatability floor** from a duplicate θ=0 cell (same seed, run twice). Values are the Planner's a-priori estimate of float32-rotation-composition noise through bf16 conditioning and a one-step sampler; the floor and the full distributions are reported regardless.
    30	  - **Tier 3 — metrics (secondary corroboration):** `Δ_C4(K)` = max−min over θ ∈ {0, 90, 180, 270}° (seed 42) and the 45° off-orbit probe; `Δ_R(K) = m_R − m_Z` seed-paired over seeds 42–46 (exp_14 random-yaw protocol). PASS if `Δ_C4` of CANON ≤ 10 % of P1's one-pin `Δ_C4` on every metric and `|Δ_R|` ≤ 1 eval-seed sd of `m_Z`.
    31	- `ε_cond` — **conditioning-level invariance (mechanism)**: max relative L2 between the vanilla conditioning tensors of `canon(md)` and `canon(rot_d(md))`, 64 real unseen items × offsets {64, 128, 256, 384, random}, fp32 (autocast off). Pre-registered PASS `≤ 1e-5` (expected ~1e-6; float32 rotation matrices). The analogue of exp_03's 4.9e-8.
    32	- **Comparator invariance (same pin, same box):** `Δ_C4` and `Δ_R` of **P1** and **YAW** re-measured at the exp_25 pin (§5), so the random-yaw comparison is a three-arm same-recipe comparison (CANON / P1 / YAW). **B-F** has fixed-angle historical cells only (exp_07 A6 / exp_17 control orbits) and is NOT part of the random-yaw comparison (review H5).
    33	- **Diagnostics** (seed 42, both K; labelled, never table rows): (i) CANON checkpoint evaluated WITHOUT canonicalization (announcement-05 protocol-mismatch cell, `--allow-canon-mismatch`); (ii) P1 checkpoint evaluated WITH canonicalization (inference-only canonicalization of a non-canonical model).
    34	- **Trajectory block (D5c, Yixun yes):** CANON checkpoints 2.5k…40k (16) × θ ∈ {0, 90, 180, 270} × K ∈ {1, 8}, seed 42 — descriptive single-seed `Δ_C4` trajectory, directly comparable to exp_17's P1 / Yaw-Aug grids (`results_yaw_aug_a6000_c4_grid_table.md`, same estimand: item-weighted, seed 42).
    35	
    36	**Hypotheses (pre-registered).**
    37	- **H-I (invariance):** Tiers 1–3 PASS for CANON at 40k (and Tier 3 at every trajectory checkpoint).
    38	- **H-Q (quality):** no direction pre-registered. Mechanism reading written before the data: canonicalization removes the yaw nuisance from training (as FA does) but (a) the canonical frame is a *discontinuous* function of the geometry — neighbouring receivers of one room can get frames far apart when the deepest direction flips, and 3.75 % of panoramas carry far-apart exact ties resolved by the equivariant rule — and (b) unlike FA it averages nothing at inference. Readout (review H7 wording): CANON ≈ B-F on `m_Z` would be *consistent with* invariance explaining part of B-F's gain over P1; CANON ≈ P1 or worse while B-F > P1 would be *consistent with* orbit averaging mattering — neither is a causal attribution (single training seed, historical control, canonicalization's own discontinuity). Either outcome is reportable.
