worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/commits_fa_orbit.md:35:| 26 | `705e308` | **B=1 breach root-caused (job 3646626)** — not a batching bug: the probe had copied train.py's global `set_float32_matmul_precision('medium')`, which turns on TF32 matmuls, and a 1-row GEMV does not take the reduced-precision GEMM path while the batched 3–31-row matmul does, so the "fp32" gate compared two DIFFERENT precisions. The breach band (3.5e-4…5.4e-4) is exactly TF32's unit roundoff 2^-11 = 4.88e-4. CPU discriminators (angle→slice mapping via a roll-encoding conditioner, and same-record B=1 vs B=8) are exact, excluding the semantic hypotheses. Fix: the gate runs in true fp32 (`highest`, cuDNN TF32 off), only the train cell keeps `medium`; precision is recorded per cell and in the result line |
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_yixun_query.md:7:> I need you to run a new experiment as a follow up of @worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_07_fa_scratch_claude/ fa_invariant conditioning and @worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/. What I need you to do is to verify this hyposithes: currently we have a consistent better result for fa FLAC @worklog/worklog_yixun/model_comparison.md , but current fa method is C4, so I want you to try C8, C16 and C32(don't need to change the other model config, data config and training config, only change the averaging over the orbit number) to see whether we can get better results with more precise equivariance/invariance to the yaw.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_yixun_query.md:11:Sweep the frame-averaging orbit size of the fa_invariant conditioning: the current fa FLAC (exp_07 B-F / exp_10 resume) averages the ViT depth-path conditioners over the C4 yaw subgroup (0/90/180/270°). Train otherwise-identical from-scratch arms at C8, C16 and C32 and test whether a finer orbit — a closer approximation to full SO(2) yaw invariance — improves on the C4 results in `model_comparison.md`.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_yixun_query.md:15:fa FLAC's consistent advantage comes from training-side yaw invariance of the conditioning (established by the exp_10 decomposition cell). C4 invariance is exact only on the 90° subgroup; averaging over a finer orbit (C8/C16/C32) makes the conditioning more precisely invariant to arbitrary yaw, which may translate into further metric gains.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_18_loc_invert_claude/paper_assets_neurips_workshop/narrative_debate_round2_reply.md:33:- The pipeline figure must devote its main panel to candidate-wise inversion: observation and context inputs → each candidate → frozen FA-FLAC with shared \(K=8\) noise bank → generated RIRs → deterministic AGREE → log-mean-exp → all-candidate argmax. A small inset must show the exact \(C_4=\{0^\circ,90^\circ,180^\circ,270^\circ\}\) group action, the actual tensor/output being averaged, shared parameters, and the boundary between training and frozen inference. Do not depict continuous yaw invariance or waveform averaging unless that is the implementation.
