worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_codex_plan_review.md:19:7. **BLOCKING — CPU/float32 synthetic tests do not establish C32 invariance under the actual bf16 path.** `invariant_conditioning` accumulates sequentially in the conditioner output dtype ([implementation](/n/fs/gatrdp/codespace/FLAC/src/data/yaw_rotation.py:294)); cyclically reordered bf16 sums are non-associative, and error can grow substantially from C4 to C32. Thus “exact invariance” may fail numerically even though the orbit is geometrically exact. **Fix:** add an actual CUDA/bf16 integration probe for C4/C8/C16/C32 using the real conditioner, testing every in-group rotation against the base output and an fp32 reference. Pre-register maximum absolute/relative tolerances and use the measured floor in D1/R3. Any change to fp32 accumulation would exceed the “angles only” treatment and therefore requires Yixun approval plus a new C4 control.
