worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/method_note_group_averaging.md:7:A mono room impulse response is physically invariant under a rigid rotation of the entire scene about the vertical axis: for any yaw angle α, rotating room geometry, source, and listener together leaves the recorded RIR unchanged. Formally, with g·x denoting the action of g ∈ SO(2) on the scene description x (panorama + poses), the ideal model satisfies **F(g·x) = F(x)** — invariance, not equivariance, because the output (a mono waveform) carries no orientation.
